    {0x00585bc8u, "RECRUITS"},
    {0x00585bd4u, "Armed with a Mark I laser rifle, a satchel charge, and an CuproSteel ablative flak jacket, Recruits are your basic cannon fodder."},
    {0x00585c58u, "GREEN UNITS"},
    {0x00585c64u, "Slightly better trained than Recruits, Green Units are equipped with Mark II lasers, which have a slightly better rate of fire and damage potential. They also carry a satchel charge and wear the CuproSteel flak jacket."},
    {0x00585d40u, "GENERAL INFANTRY"},
    {0x00585d54u, "Better training gives the General Infantry unit greater mobility under fire. They carry the Mark II laser, a satchel charge, and NuChrome reflective full-body armor."},
    {0x00585dfcu, "VETERANS"},
    {0x00585e08u, "Their training over, Veterans have earned their stripes on the killing fields. They come armed with the Mark III laser, making them more useful against Tanks in the Tech Level 1 class. Again, a satchel charge and NuChrome reflective full-body armor is standard issue."},
    {0x00585f14u, "ELITE GUARD"},
    {0x00585f20u, "These troops have learned battlefield tactics from the best, and so have the greatest mobility of any Soldier class. Not only do they carry the Mark III laser, they also sport GammaSteel full-body battle armor."},
    {0x00585ff4u, "ALPHA CLASS"},
    {0x00586000u, "An Alpha Class laser turret is an effective means of defending your bases against most low-tech enemy units."},
    {0x00586070u, "BETA CLASS"},
    {0x0058607cu, "The Beta Class laser turret can demolish all types of inbound enemy units at a greater distance and with a better rate of fire than the Alpha Class laser turret. A 5-mm CuproSteel jacket enhances the turret's durability."},
    {0x0058615cu, "GAMMA CLASS"},
    {0x00586168u, "QuadRhod armor gives this turret a decided edge against most enemy units up to tech level 4. Twin 160 kilocycle lasers provides plenty of punch."},
    {0x005861fcu, "SALVO"},
    {0x00586204u, "The Salvo SAM Site is your basic production model, providing inexpensive defense against inbound air raids."},
    {0x00586270u, "BARRAGE"},
    {0x00586278u, "The Barrage refines the design of the Salvo, delivering higher-yield rounds at an increased rate of fire."},
    {0x005862e4u, "RAKE"},
    {0x005862ecu, "The highest level of technological development, the Rake sends massive-yield tracer rounds across the sky at a rate of fire that seems incredibly unlikely."},
    {0x00586388u, "WILDCAT"},
    {0x00586390u, "The Wildcat is extremely effective against Imperium and Native Forces Soldier units, as well as being moderately effective against other Tanks. It has very little in the way of firepower, horsepower, or armor. It is armed with a 100 kilocycle laser cannon."},
    {0x00586494u, "HYENA"},
    {0x0058649cu, "The only noticeable difference between the Wildcat and the Hyena is the Hyena's durability. Its armor is ten-ply Asbesteel and NuChrome reinforced ablative armor; lighter weight than the Wildcat's armor, this somewhat increases the maximum speed of the Hyena."},
    {0x005865a0u, "CHEETAH"},
    {0x005865a8u, "The Cheetah is aptly named; its increase in mobility over the Hyena and Wildcat is quite noticeable. This is due mainly to the Cheetah's advanced CarbonWeave composite armor. It comes equipped with a 120 kilocycle main gun."},
    {0x00586688u, "LEOPARD"},
    {0x00586690u, "The leopard takes a speed hit due to its heavy QuadRhod rhodium electroplate armor, but this is more than made up for by its incredible durability. Coupled to the Leopard is a 140 kilocycle laser cannon."},
    {0x0058675cu, "PUMA"},
    {0x00586764u, "The Puma's armor is further enhanced by a dynamic repair ability that utilizes mist electroplating as an onboard system. Though this system is not 100% efficient (the armor that has been lost cannot be replaced), it is extremely fast and reliable. The 140 kilocycle laser cannon remains standard."},
    {0x00586890u, "SPITTER"},
    {0x00586898u, "The Spitter is armed with twin 160 kilocycle laser cannons"},
    {0x005868d4u, "SHRIKE"},
    {0x005868dcu, "The Shrike's laser cannons have been upgraded to the 200 kilocycle type."},
    {0x00586928u, "SARACEN"},
    {0x00586930u, "The Saracen is further upgraded with twin 240 kilocycle laser cannons; the cooling plant has also been modified to allow for a better rate of fire."},
    {0x005869c4u, "SLAMMER"},
    {0x005869ccu, "The Slammer's twin 260 kilocycle guns can knock low-tech AAVs out of the sky in one pulse."},
    {0x00586a28u, "SLAUGHTERHOUSE V"},
    {0x00586a3cu, "The ultimate in firepower, the Slaughterhouse V 300 kilocycle laser cannons can reduce medium-tech tanks and AAVs to a smoking, charred mess in a single burst."},
    {0x00586adcu, "PEACEKEEPER"},
    {0x00586ae8u, "The PeaceKeeper employs a garnet focusing crystal that causes damage with rays produced and magnified in the near-infrared spectrum. Each shot costs 900 units of power."},
    {0x00586b94u, "WARMONGER"},
    {0x00586c84u, "PUNISHER"},
    {0x00586c90u, "The ultimate KSAT building, the Punisher uses a trio of focusing crystals (sapphire, emerald, and aquamarine) within a plasma matrix to produce the most destructive power currently available. 600 units of power is required for each use."},
    {0x00586d80u, "210 tHz"},
    {0x00586d88u, "Capable of tapping only the most obvious sources of residual power."},
    {0x00586dccu, "270 tHz"},
    {0x00586dd4u, "Slightly better rate of power flow than the 210 tHz Model, this model reduces the time needed to reduce a power source to zero."},
    {0x00586e54u, "330 tHz"},
    {0x00586e5cu, "This Power building is quite effective for fast power production."},
    {0x00586ea0u, "390 tHz"},
    {0x00586ea8u, "The creme de la creme of Power Buildings, the 390 tHz Model produces power one-and-a-half times as rapidly as the 210 tHz Model."},
    {0x00586f2cu, "SPARROW"},
    {0x00586f34u, "The Sparrow is the most basic of aerial assault platforms. Moderate speed combined with minimal firepower help make the Sparrow, at best, a decent bomber-hunter, and, at worst, a distraction. It is equipped with a Grenadier missile system. A boosted Sparrow carries a single Mole Torpedo."},
    {0x00587058u, "CROW"},
    {0x00587060u, "The Crow, though still a low-tech craft, nevertheless seems to be a quantum leap over the Sparrow. A more powerful engine increases the speed, while 3-mm CuproSteel plating adds to the Crow's durability. The Grenadier missile launcher remains stock. Boosted Crows receive a Mole Torpedo and a 100 kilocycle laser."},
    {0x0058719cu, "HAWK"},
    {0x005871a4u, "The Hawk sports  Pilum missiles and a 100 kilocycle laser cannon as standard equipment. In addition, the Hawk also carries double cross-ply layers of 3-mm CuproSteel armor, reducing the damage it takes from small arms fire. Boosted Hawk receive a Mole Torpedo and 120 kilocycle laser cannon."},
    {0x005872c8u, "CONDOR"},
    {0x005872d0u, "The Puma's D-M-E armor repair system has been modified for the Condor. The weapons have been upgraded to include a 120 kilocycle laser cannon. You'll notice a marked increase in speed between the Hawk and the Condor. A boosted Condor carries a Mole Torpedo and 160 kilocycle laser cannon."},
    {0x005873f4u, "EAGLE"},
    {0x005873fcu, "A T-M-E and triple cross-ply 3-mm CuproSteel armor increases the durability of the Eagle even further. Although the cannon remains at the 140 kilocycle level, an Attila missile system replaces the Condor's pilums. Boosted Eagles get a Mole Torpedo and 160 kilocycle laser cannon."},
    {0x0058751cu, "The LR-12 almost seems to crawl across the sky, but its pinpoint accuracy with its payload of three Atlas-class bombs can bring a chill to the hearts of the enemy. Its airframe is sheathed in 1-mm CuproSteel armor. Boosted LR-12s receive a 40 kilocycle anti-AAV laser."},
    {0x00587634u, "An increase in speed is the LR-18's biggest asset over the LR-12, although the newer high-yield Titan-class bomb payload certainly doesn't hurt. A 40 kilocycle anti-AAV laser cannon is mounted on boosted LR-18s."},
    {0x00587710u, "3-mm CuproSteel armor covers a titanium-alloy airframe, resulting in a higher durability rate for the LR-23. The LR-23 can only support a deliverable payload of two Atlas-class bombs. Also standard are two countermeasures flares for deceiving heat-seeking missiles. Boosting LR-23s gives them a 40 kilocycle anti-AAV laser cannon."},
    {0x00587864u, "The LR-40 over-torqued engines serve it well. Not only is is faster than its predecessors, it can also carry a larger payload of 5 Atlas-class bombs. Standard equipment found on the LR-40 are two countermeasures flares and a 40 kilocycle anti-AAV laser cannon. LR-40s that are boosted gain the benefit of a 100-kilocycle anti-AAV laser cannon."},
    {0x005879c4u, "The undisputed heavyweight champion of the world. The LR-51's stock in trade includes a payload of 5 Armageddon-class bombs, triple cross-ply 9-mm CuproSteel armor, two countermeasures flares and twin 60 kilocycle anti-AAV laser cannons. Boosting an LR-51, though it seems somewhat unnecessary, will add a 100 kilocycle anti-AAV laser cannon."},
    {0x00587b1cu, "Convoy Truck"},
    {0x00587b2cu, "Carries Supplies."},
    {0x00587b40u, "Friendly Wraith"},
    {0x00587b50u, "Standard Chassis"},
    {0x00587b64u, "Durable and fast -- yet very expensive to replace, the wraith's light weight, reinforced chassis is both a strength and a weakness."},
    {0x00587be8u, "Reinforced Chassis"},
    {0x00587bfcu, "Provides improved armor and durability."},
    {0x00587c24u, "Advanced Chassis"},
    {0x00587c38u, "Dynamic reinforcement, miniaturizaion, and redundancy greatly improve the wraith's survivability."},
    {0x00587c9cu, "Spline Weapon"},
    {0x00587cacu, "Drains protons from your opponent and directs them towards a revitalization of your wraith."},
    {0x00587d08u, "Improved Spline Weapon"},
    {0x00587d20u, "Increased drain capacity and effectiveness improve the weapon's overall ability."},
    {0x00587d74u, "Ultra Spline Weapon"},
    {0x00587d88u, "Even greater drain capacity and a faster drain make the spline weapon a staple."},
    {0x00587dd8u, "Flame Gun"},
    {0x00587de4u, "A time - honored tradition in human warfare, the flame gun, though limited by ammunition, is one of the few weapons that damage buildings."},
    {0x00587e70u, "Flame Gun"},
    {0x00587e7cu, "More ammunition and an increase in intensity make the flame gun still more formidable."},
    {0x00587ed4u, "Flame Gun"},
    {0x00587ee0u, "Increased ammunition improves the flame gun's effectiveness."},
    {0x00587f20u, "Cupid Missile Rack"},
    {0x00587f34u, "Nicknamed the 'Katyushka' -- provides large amounts of unguided firepower."},
    {0x00587f80u, "Cupid Missile Rack II"},
    {0x00587f98u, "Increased ammunition improves the Cupid's staying power in long firefights."},
    {0x00587fe4u, "Cupid Missile Rack III"},
    {0x00587ffcu, "Better damage greatly enhances the Cupid's effectiveness."},
    {0x00588038u, "Helix Missile I"},
    {0x00588048u, "A guided, compact missile that combines good damage with accuracy."},
    {0x0058808cu, "Helix Missile II"},
    {0x005880a0u, "The increased damage more than makes up for the reduction in ammunition, improve the Helix's overall threat."},
    {0x00588110u, "Helix Missile III"},
    {0x00588124u, "Combines the firepower of the Helix II with the ammunition of the Helix I. An excellent all-around weapon."},
    {0x00588190u, "Hive Missile"},
    {0x005881a0u, "The Hive Missile is a high - yield, true - seeking weapon. The technology used for the Hive missiles is nothing like other human technology. A prototype was found in a captured Imperial compound and we can now mass produce it."},
    {0x00588284u, "BFM 9000"},
    {0x00588290u, "Extremely useful against air targets, also useful against ground units. True heat seeking makes the BFM an excellent complement to the Wraith's arsenal."},
    {0x0058832cu, "Anvil Drop"},
    {0x00588338u, "Splat!"},
    {0x00588340u, "Mortar"},
    {0x00588348u, "The only indirect fire weapon, the mortar is useful against buildings."},
    {0x00588390u, "Mortar HE"},
    {0x0058839cu, "The high explosive shell mortar increases the damage, improves the weapon's overall effectiveness."},
    {0x00588400u, "Mortar HEAP"},
    {0x0058840cu, "The High - explosive shells are combined in with an armor piercing shell, allowing the shell to further penetrate a building's armor before exploding."},
    {0x005884a4u, "Automatic Mine Layer I"},
    {0x005884bcu, "Deposits a mine laying drone which will dispense 14 mines and then disintegrate. To use this weapon, you need to posses mine technology as well"},
    {0x0058854cu, "Automatic Mine Layer II"},
    {0x00588564u, "The AML II's drone lays 20 mines as opposed to the AML I's 14."},
    {0x005885a4u, "Mole Torpedo"},
    {0x005885b4u, "Perfect for undermining turrets and clearing minefields and slow-moving infantry, the mole torpedo is limited greatly by it's velocity."},
    {0x0058863cu, "Mole Torpedo II"},
    {0x0058864cu, "Faster Torpedoes and a higher carrying capacity improve it's viability as a main weapon"},
    {0x005886a4u, "Mole Torpedo III"},
    {0x005886b8u, "Better damage and even more ammo make the Mole Torpedo II the ultimate weapon!"},
    {0x00588708u, "100 k-cycle gatling laser"},
    {0x00588724u, "A staple of the wraith's arsenal. Excellent against most ground targets."},
    {0x00588770u, "109 k-cycle gatling laser"},
    {0x0058878cu, "Improved laser output translates to better damage down field."},
    {0x005887ccu, "123 k-cycle gatling laser"},
    {0x005887e8u, "Pushing the upper-limits of the wraith's coolant capacity, the 123-k set to maximum firepower will annihilate almost anything short of a building."},
    {0x0058887cu, "Alpha-Class, Limited HSM"},
    {0x00588898u, "Another staple of the wraith's arsenal. Excellent against most ground targets and air targets on strafe runs."},
    {0x00588908u, "Beta-Class, Limited HSM"},
    {0x00588920u, "Improved damage, rate of fire, and range increase the LHSM's effectiveness."},
    {0x0058896cu, "Gamma-Class Limited HSM"},
    {0x00588984u, "Much greater damage and range increase the Gamma missile's stopping power."},
    {0x005889d0u, "Antimatter Disk Lv 1"},
    {0x005889e8u, "Using TerraTech technology, it spins across the terrain, leaving a wake of destruction."},
    {0x00588a40u, "Antimatter Disk Lv 2"},
    {0x00588a58u, "Better antimatter containment allows a larger payload, increasing the weapon's damage."},
    {0x00588ab0u, "Antimatter Disk Lv 3"},
    {0x00588ac8u, "A more efficient conversion of matter / antimatter to energy increases the disk's punch."},
    {0x00588b24u, "Land Mine"},
    {0x00588b30u, "Equipped with IFF technology, you and your units are safe from land mine's you've placed."},
    {0x00588b8cu, "Land Mine II"},
    {0x00588b9cu, "Greatly improved ammunition makes the mine layer much more convenient."},
    {0x00588be4u, "Land Mine III"},
    {0x00588bf4u, "Better ammunitiona nd a cheaper mine allow the user to greatly increase his/her mine laying."},
    {0x00588c54u, "Basic Remote repair"},
    {0x00588c68u, "A single repair module which will repair about two thirds of the standard Wraith chassis."},
    {0x00588cc4u, "Remote repair"},
    {0x00588cd4u, "A double repair module which will repair over two thirds of the standard Wraith chassis."},
    {0x00588d30u, "Advanced Remote repair"},
    {0x00588d48u, "A triple repair module which will repair about three quarters of the standard Wraith chassis."},
    {0x00588da8u, "Ultra Remote repair"},
    {0x00588dbcu, "A four ammo repair module which will repair over three quarters of the standard Wraith chassis."},
